# Avatar Destiny: "Return this card to its owner's hand and up to one creature card milled this way to the battlefield under your control."
# As in the Bolt scenario the Bears die on turn 4 wearing it (3/3, one creature card in Bot1's graveyard) and the trigger goes on the stack.
# In response Bot2 exiles the Aura from Bot1's graveyard with Cling to Dust: it is a new object (CR 400.7), so the trigger returns nothing
# (the 2011-09-22 Angelic Destiny ruling) while it still mills three cards. Bot1 chooses no creature card ("up to one"): Giant Spider and
# Hill Giant stay in the graveyard, the Destiny stays in exile and Bot1's hand is only its Island.

